# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this template is not.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS PUBLIC. Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the JavaScript it
# ships, so these values are readable by anyone with DevTools. That is fine for
# what is listed below -- a PostHog project key is write-only, meant to sit in
# the browser, and can do nothing but send events in. Never put a real secret
# behind the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix; a secret that the site can read is not one.
#
# The deploy is a GitHub Action, which never sees .env.local. Anything added
# here also has to be added as a repository secret and passed through in
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml, or production builds silently go without it.

# PostHog project API key -- Project Settings, under "Project API Key".
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# EU cloud by default: the audience is American and European, and keeping EU
# visitors' events on EU infrastructure is the simpler side of GDPR to argue.
# US cloud is https://us.i.posthog.com -- it must match the region the project
# was created in, or events are accepted and then dropped on the floor.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
